## Macro Database Ownership And Layout Pass

Problem: `H8MacroDatabaseService._blackBox` was a live 300-frame `NativeArray<MacroDatabaseTelemetryEntry>` without Sentinel ownership, and stale status text incorrectly said it had already been registered. Directly referencing `Hecton8.Core.NativeMemorySentinel` from `Hecton8.Core.Database` would create an asmdef cycle because root Core already references Database.
Solution: Added `NativeMemoryTrackingBridge` in `Hecton8.Core.Contracts`, added a root Core installer that routes the bridge to `NativeMemorySentinel`, and registered/unregistered `_blackBox` through that bridge after cold allocation / before dispose. Existing `SectorCoord64` / `HydrationCandidate` natural sequential layouts with explicit `Size = 24` and `Size = 48` remain aligned.
Rejected Alternatives: A direct Database -> Core asmdef reference was rejected as a compile wall. Migrating the macro database blackbox to GlobalDataVault in this pass was rejected because it changes service ownership during external compile-wall churn. Leaving private runtime `Pack=1` was rejected by the ARM64 mandate.
Scalability potential: Low = cleaner ARM64 native scratch layout and leak-visible blackbox ownership. Middle = better long-session database telemetry. High/Ultra = future Vault migration has a bounded source.
Hardware Impact: 0 us hot path. Registration/unregister is cold lifecycle work only. Full audit hard errors dropped 7 -> 6.

